swf1file
========

Turn any Flash .swf into ONE html file. No server, no network, no
sidecar files. Double-click, play. Works from file:// in every modern
browser that runs WebAssembly.

    src/build.mjs          the packer: swf + ruffle -> one .html
    scripts/get-ruffle.mjs vendor the ruffle core (MIT/Apache)
    tests/verify.mjs       build a toy swf, check the output

How it works
------------

Ruffle loads its wasm core by URL. From file:// that URL does not
resolve, so a small fetch shim answers the request from bytes embedded
in the page itself:

    the swf        base64 -> Blob URL -> player.load()
    ruffle.js      inlined verbatim
    core wasm x2   SIMD build + baseline build, base64 -> Blob
    fetch shim     intercepts "./ruffle_web*.wasm", serves the blobs

No patching of ruffle.js. Nothing on disk except the html you ship.

Usage
-----

    node scripts/get-ruffle.mjs        # once, fetches ruffle release
    node src/build.mjs game.swf        # -> game.html

See INSTALL for details.

Not a piracy kit
----------------

This tool ships NO games. You supply the swf; you own the
consequences. Nintendo and McLeodGaming did not bless anything here.
Classic Flash games are abandonware in practice and copyrighted in
law; keep your output personal.

